discover.prompt:
Below is the content of any existing Dockerfiles found in this repository:
{existing_dockerfiles}

Base image hint from the user: {base_image_hint}

Identify whether any existing Dockerfile in this repo already establishes a base image that the new Dockerfile should share, for build-cache and consistency reasons. Respond with exactly one line: either "SHARED_BASE: <image:tag>" citing the file it came from, or "NO_SHARED_BASE" if none of the existing Dockerfiles are a good match or none exist. No other text.

audit.prompt:
Security-audit the following proposed Dockerfile content (path-bearing fence(s)):
{dockerfile_reply}

Check specifically for: running as root in any stage meant to serve traffic, use of :latest or unpinned base image tags, secrets/credentials embedded as ARG or ENV literals, unnecessary build toolchain or dev dependencies leaking into a non-dev final stage, overly broad COPY (e.g. "COPY . ." pulling in .git, .env, node_modules, credentials files) instead of explicit paths or a .dockerignore reference, and missing HEALTHCHECK for long-running service stages. List every issue found, one per line, with the stage name and a one-sentence fix. If there are none, write exactly: NO ISSUES FOUND.

Findings from a Dockerfile security audit:
{audit_findings}

Respond with exactly one word: PASS if the findings are exactly "NO ISSUES FOUND" or contain nothing that is an actual security or correctness defect, otherwise FAIL. No other text.

gate.prompt:
Security audit FAILED for {dockerfile_path}:
{audit_findings}

Type FORCE to write the Dockerfile anyway, or STOP to abort without writing so the issues can be addressed first.
